      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The current workaround I've found most convenient is performance blocking avatars, going to an user's profile, then navigating to the big new \"Avatar Details\" with tags/styles/galleries and checking the logs for a sample line like this:\n\n```\n\n2026.01.17 00:00:00 Debug      -  Loading Avatar Data:avtr_67676767-6767-6767-6767-676767676767\n\n```\n\nIf the avatar was already loaded and not performance blocked, then performance block all avatars and rejoin the instance, and repeat the steps. No report API required.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
